  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want to open an image full screen and swipe through the images of the page, so that I see them in high resolution.\n\n### Scope\n\nViewer with zoom, swipe between images of the page, hi-res URL from the host table (LOT-056), save to Photos, share, copy link.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-014 (#158)\n- Absorbs: FEAT-014; user feedback gallery lost / blurry thumbnails (≈21)\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `Classes/SimplePhotoViewController.m`, `MessagesView.swift` (`MessageImagePhotoLibrarySaver`, `PhotoViewerDestination`)\n- Spec: `docs/features/FEAT-014.md` (feature spec, ADR 0011 §2; write it first if absent, crediting Bybifok) plus a short `docs/lots/LOT-109-*.md` pointing to it\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-083 (#101, in-progress)\n- LOT-056 (#82, ready)\n- LOT-160 (#250)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged. Capture #134 is still pending, and the operator decided on 2026-10-29 that the lot starts anyway with it listed as *pending capture*. The check against the capture is review #328.\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-014 (#158), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: none; **this lot is the last one: its PR also says `Closes #158`**.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- #134\n\n### Capture first if you can\n\n- **CLI session with capture access** (the maintainer's Mac, LOT-001 kit): do capture #134 before the lot.\n- **Any other session:** build on legacy and the LOT-056 host table, and list #134 as *pending capture* in the spec.\n- **Either way:** post one comment on review #328 saying what you did: the capture PR and fixture ids, or what the lot assumes, with the legacy file:line.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Image requests follow D-071-1 (cookie-less, Referer only per host table); close button reachable on iPad.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
